{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733824",
      "title": "Module Introduction",
      "sourceHash": "56f4961ab8a1dd83139a3eefc0c11e2a5bf3d3ca8cf88ba09345ee5fb76331ed",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "At this point in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "we already learned a lot about React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "and we built a couple of demo applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 11.509,
          "en": "But there's one characteristic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.509,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "which all demo applications shared,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "everything happened on one single page in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "Sure, the user interface changed from time to time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "upon certain actions, but it was all on one page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "and the URL therefore never changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 30.18,
          "en": "It was always the same URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.18,
          "end": 32.193,
          "en": "no matter what happened on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "And indeed, that is one of the core ideas behind React.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "that you can use it to build single page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.9,
          "en": "applications where client side JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.9,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "takes care about changing what the user sees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 48.183,
          "en": "and it's technically always the same page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "Now that has its advantages, but it also has disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 57.84,
          "en": "Most importantly, we lose one of the biggest advantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.84,
          "end": 61.02,
          "en": "of the web, the advantage that we can link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "to certain resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 66.303,
          "en": "Because the more complex your applications get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.19800000000001,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "the more you might want to be able to link to certain parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 74.07,
          "en": "of your website and your web application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.07,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "Instead of forcing users to always start on the start page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "and then navigate to different areas manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "it would be nice if users could be linked to certain pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 89.46000000000001,
          "en": "if you could provide a URL that loads a certain part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.46000000000001,
          "end": 91.773,
          "en": "of your website when visited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "After all, that is how most websites work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "And at the moment, in our React applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.533,
          "en": "we lost this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "That's where single page application routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 105.6,
          "en": "comes into play,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.6,
          "end": 109.02000000000001,
          "en": "and where this course section becomes important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.02000000000001,
          "end": 111.03,
          "en": "Because in this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.03,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "you will learn how you can still build React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "applications that are technically single page applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 121.02,
          "en": "So where we don't fetch new pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "from some backend all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "and you can still have different URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "leading to different pages, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 132.39,
          "en": "of your overall website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 134.7,
          "en": "So that you get the best of both worlds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "you can still build a single page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 139.23,
          "en": "as you will see throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.23,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "You can leverage all your React knowledge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 144.78,
          "en": "and yet you can have different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.78,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "with different URLs to which you can forward users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 152.16,
          "en": "and which can be loaded by inserting the right URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "in the browser address bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "And therefore, in this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 159.96,
          "en": "you will learn what exactly client side routing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.96,
          "end": 162.57,
          "en": "and how it works and why you might want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 164.88,
          "en": "Though I, of course, already touched on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.88,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "over the last couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "You will then learn how to use a package called React-Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 174.347,
          "en": "which is the most popular routing package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.347,
          "end": 176.73,
          "en": "for React applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.73,
          "end": 180.09,
          "en": "which is a package that allows us to bring back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 184.83,
          "en": "that multi page feeling to our single page React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "And later in this section, we'll also dive into fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 192.63,
          "en": "and sending data, and we'll learn how React-Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "can help us with that and how it can actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 199.113,
          "en": "simplify the process of fetching and sending data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}